[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3524024116","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112668#issuecomment-3524024116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112668","id":3524024116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SDFc0","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-12T21:34:38Z","updated_at":"2025-11-12T21:34:38Z","body":"> The Profiler does not show which function the lag is coming from, but the Monitor correctly displays the process time.\n\nThe profiler does show which script functions are running and which ones are causing significant time spikes. Do you mean the fact that there is a huge time discrepancy between the reported script time and total process time? If yes, it could just be that the lag spike occurs in engine code, and not game code.\n\n<img width=\"1364\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c60dfacb-2211-4ef1-bb07-3c0418374c42\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/co